From: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] brcmfmac: pcie: BCM4360 phase5 test instrumentation (T276/T277/T278/T298/T305/T306)

BCM4360 bring-up instrumentation ported from kimptoc/bcm4360-re
phase5 (base v6.12; the reference tree only contains T276/277/278/298;
T305/T306 were specified in RESUME_NOTES design docs and the
fire-t305-t306.sh script). Six module params, all default 0 and gated
on chip == BRCM_CC_4360_CHIP_ID, so every other chip's behaviour is
unchanged:

- bcm4360_test276_shared_info: write a shared_info handshake struct at
  TCM[ramsize-0x2F5C] (magic 0xA5A5A5A5) plus a 64 KiB olmsg DMA ring
  buffer before ARM release, then poll the response fields for 2 s
  post-release.
- bcm4360_test277_console_decode: dump the 4-dword console struct at
  the fw-published pointer (pre-write snapshot at 0x9af88, post-poll
  at si[+0x010]) plus 128 B of the console buffer.
- bcm4360_test278_console_periodic: seed the console-delta cursor with
  a full dump, then periodic delta dumps at t+500ms, t+5s, t+30s,
  t+90s.
- bcm4360_test298_isr_walk: BAR2-only walk of the RTE scheduler ISR
  list at TCM[0x629A4] + sched_ctx[+0xCC] + pending-events word, at
  each stage.
- bcm4360_test305_premask_with_select: pre-set_active MAILBOXMASK
  enable WITH explicit select_core(PCIE2) before
  brcmf_pcie_intr_enable (bcmdhd si_corereg pattern); logs
  BAR0_WINDOW before/after, MBM pre/post and a SUMMARY verdict
  (WRITE_LANDED/WRITE_DROPPED/UNEXPECTED_VALUE).
- bcm4360_test306_cfg_dump: read-only PCI config dump 0x40..0xFF
  (48 dwords) at 3 stages (pre-set_active/post-set_active/
  post-T276-poll), highlighting the vendor area 0x94/0xB4/0xB8.

Adaptations for 7.1.8: the reference restructured download_fw_nvram
(moved the brcmf_chip_set_active call out of exit_download_state);
7.1.8 keeps the upstream structure, so the pre-release block hooks
between the NVRAM write and exit_download_state(), and the
post-release block (2 s poll, T277 decode, T306 stages 2-3, T278/T298
ladder) hooks right after exit_download_state() returns. The
reference's 120 s test.238 dwell ladder is reduced to the four
T278/T298 stages the fire script actually uses. T305/T306 did not
exist in the reference tree; they are implemented from the
RESUME_NOTES design specs, wired into the pre-set_active block per
the fire script's description, each gated on its own param. Two
forward declarations (brcmf_pcie_select_core, brcmf_pcie_intr_enable)
are added for the T305 probe, which sits ahead of their definitions.

Signed-off-by: OpenWiFi BCM4360 Project <bcm4360@localhost>
